import{_ as i,o as n,c as a,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const y=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 885 | Transcended Ones and Law | The Transcended One's Legal Liability","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 885 | Transcended Ones and Law | The Transcended One's Legal Liability","no":885,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Law","Legal Liability","Accountability","Compensation"],"related":["48-Judicial System and Adjudication Mechanism","40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline","884-Legal Constraints on the Transcended One","887-The Transcended One's Legal-Exemption Boundaries"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0885_模块4-超脱者与法律-法律责任.md","filePath":"en/0885_模块4-超脱者与法律-法律责任.md"}`),o={name:"en/0885_模块4-超脱者与法律-法律责任.md"};function r(s,e,l,d,h,c){return n(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="entry-885-transcended-ones-and-law-the-transcended-one-s-legal-liability" tabindex="-1">Entry 885 | Transcended Ones and Law | The Transcended One&#39;s Legal Liability <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-885-transcended-ones-and-law-the-transcended-one-s-legal-liability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 885 | Transcended Ones and Law | The Transcended One&#39;s Legal Liability&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 48, 40, 884, 887</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-you-do-wrong-you-take-responsibility-—-even-if-you-are-the-transcended-one" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when you do wrong, you take responsibility — even if you are the transcended one <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-you-do-wrong-you-take-responsibility-—-even-if-you-are-the-transcended-one" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when you do wrong, you take responsibility — even if you are the transcended one&quot;">​</a></h2><p>When the old world&#39;s strong ones do wrong, the cost is borne by Myriad Ranks. A Great Emperor fails his tribulation; stars collapse, billions buried with him, then he awakens and continues as Great Emperor. No one asked him: for the loss caused by your tribulation failure, who pays? Heng Yuan Zhou must make clear: <strong>when the transcended one does wrong, he himself is responsible — compensation, penalty, demotion, even qualification revocation.</strong> This entry explains the transcended one&#39;s legal-liability system.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously take the stage: the anti-predation axiom requires liability not be shifted to the weak; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires liability apply to all beings; the collective ascension axiom requires the liability mechanism serve civilizational repair; the causal self-discipline axiom requires liability tracing be enforceable; the law-first axiom requires liability laws be self-consistent, not excused by person; the universal equal infinite law confirms all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; easygoing layabouts retain a floor and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher infinity — infinite origin is inherent in all, predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-three-types-of-legal-liability" tabindex="-1">I. Three Types of Legal Liability <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-three-types-of-legal-liability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Three Types of Legal Liability&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-civil-liability" tabindex="-1">1. Civil liability <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-civil-liability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1. Civil liability&quot;">​</a></h3><p>When the transcended one&#39;s behavior causes another party&#39;s loss, he bears compensation:</p><ul><li>Damaged some plane&#39;s environment → responsible for repair or equivalent compensation;</li><li>Interfered with some cultivator&#39;s breakthrough process → provide compensatory resources;</li><li>Due to negligence caused public-facility damage → responsible for repair.</li></ul><h3 id="_2-administrative-liability" tabindex="-1">2. Administrative liability <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-administrative-liability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2. Administrative liability&quot;">​</a></h3><p>When the transcended one violates post duties or administrative regulations, he bears administrative penalty:</p><ul><li>Warning, demerit, deduction of civilizational weight;</li><li>Suspension of post authority, forced rotation;</li><li>Demotion (from a Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm post to a lower post).</li></ul><h3 id="_3-criminal-liability" tabindex="-1">3. Criminal liability <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-criminal-liability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3. Criminal liability&quot;">​</a></h3><p>When the transcended one violates criminal law, he bears criminal penalty:</p><ul><li>Touching red lines (the seven red lines in entry 884);</li><li>Serious dereliction causing major Myriad-Rank loss;</li><li>Conspiring to usurp power, colluding with predatory schools.</li></ul><h2 id="ii-the-alaya-basis-of-liability-tracing" tabindex="-1">II. The Alaya Basis of Liability Tracing <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-alaya-basis-of-liability-tracing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Alaya Basis of Liability Tracing&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s liability tracing relies on Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s full-process trace. This ensures:</p><ul><li><strong>Facts clear</strong>: what the transcended one did, when, and what consequences, the Alaya Network all records;</li><li><strong>Complete evidence chain</strong>: no need for the transcended one to &quot;confess himself&quot;; Alaya records are ironclad evidence;</li><li><strong>Non-deniable</strong>: the transcended one may not &quot;have forgotten&quot; or &quot;do not remember&quot; — the Alaya Network remembers;</li><li><strong>Non-falsifiable</strong>: the transcended one may not modify or delete records unfavorable to himself.</li></ul><p>Alaya supervision makes liability tracing precise and efficient. The old world&#39;s difficulty holding the strong accountable was because &quot;no one could say clearly what he did&quot; — in Heng Yuan Zhou this problem does not exist.</p><h2 id="iii-how-liability-is-borne" tabindex="-1">III. How Liability Is Borne <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-how-liability-is-borne" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. How Liability Is Borne&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s way of bearing liability is not simple &quot;lock up&quot; — his ability is too great, locking him is neither possible nor necessary:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Severity of Liability</th><th>Way of Bearing</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Minor negligence</td><td>Verbal warning + remedial repair + on-record</td></tr><tr><td>Ordinary negligence</td><td>Deduct civilizational weight + suspend partial authority + retraining</td></tr><tr><td>Serious negligence</td><td>Demotion + rotation + compensate loss</td></tr><tr><td>Intentional illegality</td><td>Revoke transcended-one qualification + withdraw post authority + criminal trial</td></tr><tr><td>Collusion with predatory schools</td><td>Revoke qualification + permanently strip cultivation right + maximum penalty</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Liability&#39;s core principle is: <strong>repair the damage, correct the behavior, prevent recurrence.</strong> It is not punishment for punishment&#39;s sake, but for restoring the system to normal.</p><h2 id="iv-liability-s-binding-with-post" tabindex="-1">IV. Liability&#39;s Binding with Post <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-liability-s-binding-with-post" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Liability&#39;s Binding with Post&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s legal liability is tightly bound to his post:</p><ul><li><strong>Mistakes within post scope</strong>: follow post-responsibility procedure, lighter or mitigated;</li><li><strong>Illegal behavior outside post scope</strong>: follow ordinary legal procedure, no mitigation;</li><li><strong>Crimes using post authority</strong>: heavier penalty — because he used the trust Myriad Ranks granted.</li></ul><p>This binding ensures the transcended one may not say &quot;I was working&quot; to excuse his own illegal behavior. Work mistakes and intentional crimes, the law distinguishes clearly.</p><p>The ultimate purpose of liability pursuit is not to punish the transcended one, but to repair the system. Compensate loss, correct behavior, prevent recurrence — if these three steps are in place, the transcended one may continue working; if not, it escalates to qualification revocation. The law is not meant to lock the transcended one up, but to let him continue being a responsible transcended one.</p><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s trace makes liability pursuit no longer depend on confession. The transcended one may deny his own behavior, but he cannot deny the Alaya records. This ironclad tracing ability is itself a constraint on the transcended one — he knows everything he does is on record, so he does not dare overstep lightly.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the liability mechanism prevents the transcended one from wasting Myriad-Rank resources because &quot;no one will hold me accountable anyway&quot;</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: when you do wrong you are responsible, not shifting to Myriad Ranks, cutting the predatory chain of &quot;the strong err, the weak pay&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo does wrong and Myriad Ranks are buried with him, he himself takes no responsibility; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s transcended one does wrong and compensates himself and is penalized himself</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the liability mechanism applies to all transcended ones, no exemption by clan or contribution</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: liability-pursuit records, judgment reasons, and compensation execution all open network-wide through the Selfless Dao</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>When the transcended one does wrong he is responsible. Civil compensation, administrative sanction, criminal penalty — according to behavior nature and consequence severity, one-to-one correspondence. Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision ensures facts clear, evidence ironclad, non-deniable. Liability is not mitigated because you are strong, nor exempted because your contribution is great. When the strongest also must pay for his own behavior, the law is no longer a paper exercise. This is the orthodox definition of the transcended one&#39;s legal liability.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/48-司法体系与裁决机制.html">Entry 48 · Judicial System and Adjudication Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/40-共生宪法总纲.html">Entry 40 · Symbiotic Constitution General Outline</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/884_模块4-超脱者与法律-法律约束.html">Entry 884 · Legal Constraints on the Transcended One</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/887_模块4-超脱者与法律-法律豁免边界.html">Entry 887 · The Transcended One&#39;s Legal-Exemption Boundaries</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',36)])])}const p=i(o,[["render",r]]);export{y as __pageData,p as default};
